load @term/seed/space/hyperbolic/horosphere
  find horosphere

# The infinigon (or apeirogon), the strangest tile: a regular polygon with infinitely many sides, inscribed not in a
# circle but in a horocycle, a circle whose center has fled to the boundary, a circle of infinite radius. The hyperbolic
# plane can be tiled with infinigons (infinigrids). A single infinigon offers infinitely many neighbors, an infinite
# resource packed into one tile, which is exactly what Margenstern's super-Turing (hypercomputation) model exploits at
# the end of the work. The form carries the horocycle the infinigon is inscribed in.
form infinigon
  link horocycle, like horosphere
